now that xiang chi has stepped up to  take his place in the marvel cinematic  universe there's no better time to get  the lowdown on the villains and rogues  he's faced over the years from mighty  crime lords to international assassins  these are shang chi's biggest foes  ever since his debut in 1973's special  marvel edition number 15 chongqi's one  true archenemy has always been his evil  scheming father in the 70s the so-called  kung fu craze reached america's shores  so marvel decided to purchase the comic  book rights to sax romer's fuumon chew  novels and created chongqi as his  previously unknown son fu manchu was the  racist xenophobic personification of  yellow peril the western fear that asian  immigrants would eventually wipe out  white culture around the world marvel  used the loss of the rights to romer's  creations as an opportunity to establish  a new backstory for chongqi's father one  that attempted to distance the villain  from his racist roots resurrected and  renamed zhang zhu in 2010's secret  avengers number eight the master of kung  fu's father was now an immortal wizard  who sought to conquer the world using  his vast criminal cult the five weapons  society the original zoo remained shang  chi's biggest enemy until his first  death in master of kung fu number 118  though the character would make several  brief returns in the years that followed  after shang qi rebelled against his  father zhang zhu sent his adopted son  the midnight son to bring him back one  way or another the adoptive brothers  clashed in special marvel edition number  16 fighting a fierce battle that  ultimately ended in tragedy midnight  sun's real name was monae and he was the  only survivor of a british assault on  his village wishing to cultivate the  hate within him zhang zhu adopted the  boy and raised him alongside shang chi  though the two men loved each other  deeply midnight's son was more loyal to  his father than he was to shang chi and  their duel only ended when monae died  after falling off a construction crane  though he was killed in his first  appearance minaj would prove to be the  first of many siblings who would become  shan chi's enemy  originally one of saks roamer's  problematic fu manchu characters follow  c's name was changed to zhang bao once  marvel lost to the rights the daughter  of zhang zhu bao yu was shang chi's half  sister and although the two sought to  defeat their father they wanted to do so  for completely different reasons while  chongqi wanted to bring an end to zoo's  criminal empire and the destruction it  caused around the globe bau wished to  supplant their father and claim his  empire for herself value debuted in  1975's master of kung fu number 26 in  which she butted heads with shang chi  for the first time for a period she also  managed to gain control of mi6 causing  chongqi and his many spy allies to leave  the agency and create an independent spy  agency called freelance restorations  introduced in 1975's giant size master  of kung fu number four the outsider  known only as tiger claw approached  zhang zhu and demanded that the villain  make him a lodge master one of the top  ranking members of the celestial order  of the siphon his private society of  assassins angered by the strangers in  pertinence zhu sent three siphon lodge  masters to kill him but tigerclaw killed  them instead convinced that he might  have finally found a match for chongqi  zoo allowed tigerclaw to replace the men  he had killed and become a lodgemaster  himself zeus hopes would soon be dashed  however confident in large part due to  his new position the lodge master  challenged the son of zhongzu to a duel  though the fight was fierce tiger claw  was decisively defeated by the  undisputed master of kung fu  the first villain known as razer fist  was simply an enhanced bodyguard named  william young who worked for a crime  lord named carlton velcro when chongqi  and this first razor fist finally met in  the field of battle velcro's guards  accidentally shot and killed him while  trying to hit xiang chi years later  velcro decided to create two new racer  fists when two of his men brothers  william and douglas scott each lost a  hand in a car accident unfortunately  william ultimately died in the same  manner as his namesake when velcro  accidentally shot and killed him this  left douglas scott as the sole remaining  razor fist douglas reappeared several  times over the years and has even come  to blows with a number of other marvel  superheroes  knowing he would never be able to  dismantle his father's vast empire on  his own sean chi soon began working with  mi6  bond  james bond one of these agents was a man  named simon brettner after spending  years working as a secret agent for mi6  brettner began developing a dual  personality named mordillo who quickly  became one of the world's most dangerous  assassins when chongqi inadvertently  kept mordillo from finishing a contract  he vowed revenge on the kung fu master  hatching a plot against his very own  teammates brettner's fellow agent laiko  wu eventually discovered his treachery  and helped mi6 track bretner to his  secret island hideout where the villain  equipped his most dangerous weapon the  death head a steel gauntlet that could  shoot fire and poison darts from its  fingertips death hand proved himself a  worthy opponent for chongqi but the  villain was ultimately incinerated when  he accidentally leapt directly into the  path of a laser weapon  introduced in master of kung fu number  42 in 1976 lancaster sneed adopted the  name shockwave after he used metal  plates to rebuild himself in the wake of  a horrific injury in the process he  vowed revenge on those he believed were  responsible for his injuries mi6  shockwave attacked mi6 and used his  specialized armor to give even seongchi  a run for his money the armor granted  sneed an incredible amount of protection  gave him a slight boost in speed  strength 